---
layout: null
---
{%- comment -%}
  THE SITEMAP, WITH A LAST-MODIFIED DATE WHEREVER THE REPOSITORY STORES ONE.

  jekyll-sitemap writes its own sitemap only when the site has none, so this file replaces the
  plugin's template and nothing else: the plugin still writes robots.txt, which names this file.
  The URL set is the plugin's, rule for rule: every output collection document, every HTML page,
  and every static .htm / .html / .xhtml / .pdf file, each unless its front matter says
  sitemap: false, and never /404.html. scripts/ci/verify_publication_hygiene.py reads the result.

  WHY. The plugin dates a page only from a last_modified_at field no page here carries, so 5 of
  1,769 URLs had a date and a crawler could not tell a patch page that changed yesterday from one
  untouched since 2019.

  WHERE A DATE COMES FROM. Only from stored data, never from the clock and never from a file's
  modification time (on the deploy runner that is the checkout time, which is the build time):
    - a patch record: its record_last_updated, the moment a writer last changed the record, or
      the release date update_published_at for the few records written before that field existed;
    - a product, company or version tracker: the newest record_last_updated among the records
      the tracker lists (same product_id, company_id, or product_id and update_version);
    - a post or other collection document: its last_modified_at, or the date its front matter or
      file name states. Jekyll gives a document with no date of its own the build time as its
      date, which is why /about/ and /articles/ used to carry the moment of the last deploy as
      their lastmod; a date equal to the build time is not a stored date and is not printed;
    - any other page: its last_modified_at when the front matter states one.
  A URL with no stored date gets no lastmod element. That is the honest reading of "unknown":
  the homepage, the Patch Feed pages and the methodology page are in that group, and so is
  every static file, whose only date is the file time this template refuses to print.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9 http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9/sitemap.xsd" xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- assign sm_collections = site.collections | where_exp: 'collection', 'collection.output != false' -%}
{%- for sm_collection in sm_collections -%}
{%- assign sm_docs = sm_collection.docs | where_exp: 'doc', 'doc.sitemap != false' -%}
{%- for sm_doc in sm_docs -%}
{%- assign sm_doc_lastmod = sm_doc.last_modified_at | default: '' -%}
{%- if sm_doc_lastmod == '' and sm_doc.date and sm_doc.date != site.time -%}{%- assign sm_doc_lastmod = sm_doc.date -%}{%- endif %}
<url>
<loc>{{ sm_doc.url | replace: '/index.html', '/' | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc>
{%- if sm_doc_lastmod != '' %}
<lastmod>{{ sm_doc_lastmod | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
{%- endif %}
</url>
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign sm_records = site.pages | where: 'update_entry', true -%}
{%- assign sm_by_product = sm_records | group_by: 'product_id' -%}
{%- assign sm_by_company = sm_records | group_by: 'company_id' -%}
{%- assign sm_pages = site.html_pages | where_exp: 'doc', 'doc.sitemap != false' | where_exp: 'doc', 'doc.url != "/404.html"' -%}
{%- for sm_page in sm_pages -%}
{%- assign sm_lastmod = '' -%}
{%- if sm_page.update_entry == true -%}
  {%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_page.record_last_updated | default: sm_page.update_published_at | default: '' -%}
{%- elsif sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-product' or sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-company' or sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-version' -%}
  {%- assign sm_listed = '' | split: '' -%}
  {%- if sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-company' -%}
    {%- assign sm_group = sm_by_company | where: 'name', sm_page.company_id | first -%}
    {%- if sm_group -%}{%- assign sm_listed = sm_group.items -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign sm_group = sm_by_product | where: 'name', sm_page.product_id | first -%}
    {%- if sm_group -%}
      {%- assign sm_listed = sm_group.items -%}
      {%- if sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-version' -%}{%- assign sm_listed = sm_listed | where: 'update_version', sm_page.update_version -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign sm_newest = 0 -%}
  {%- for sm_record in sm_listed -%}
    {%- assign sm_stamp = sm_record.record_last_updated | default: '' -%}
    {%- if sm_stamp != '' -%}
      {%- assign sm_seconds = sm_stamp | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
      {%- if sm_seconds > sm_newest -%}{%- assign sm_newest = sm_seconds -%}{%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_stamp -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- elsif sm_page.last_modified_at -%}
  {%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_page.last_modified_at -%}
{%- endif %}
<url>
<loc>{{ sm_page.url | replace: '/index.html', '/' | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc>
{%- if sm_lastmod != '' %}
<lastmod>{{ sm_lastmod | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
{%- endif %}
</url>
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for sm_file in site.static_files -%}
{%- if sm_file.extname == '.htm' or sm_file.extname == '.html' or sm_file.extname == '.xhtml' or sm_file.extname == '.pdf' -%}
{%- unless sm_file.sitemap == false or sm_file.name == '404.html' %}
<url>
<loc>{{ sm_file.path | replace: '/index.html', '/' | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc>
</url>
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
